        ],
        "text": "A man with long dark wavy hair under a black baseball cap, his two eyes glowing bright gold, glowing translucent circuit-lit forearms and hands, wearing a black t-shirt printed with the bold words DEITCH BEATS DON'T QUIT between two red mushrooms and gold circuit lines, standing in a red sandstone canyon. He holds still, his arms staying exactly where they are, as he disintegrates: his body dries into cracked grey ash from his hands and shoulders inward, the ash breaks into flakes and glowing orange embers, and a steady wind carries the flakes away to the left in a streaming cloud. His fingers, arms and legs crumble away first and his body loses volume from the edges inward, ragged holes opening through it, until only his head is left, his two eyes still glowing until they go out and the last ash blows away. The canyon behind him stays unchanged, framing never changes. Photoreal, cinematic, fine detail"
